\section{Importing array data}{

Detection-history data from \code{unmarked::unmarkedFrameOccu},
\code{unmarkedFrameOccuMulti}, \code{spOccupancy}, \code{ubms}, and \code{flocker}
arrives as a 2D \verb{[J, K]} matrix, 3D \verb{[N, J, K]} array, 4D
\verb{[N, J, T, K]} array (multi-season), or named list of \verb{[J, K]}
matrices per species. Use \code{\link[=pivot_detection_array]{pivot_detection_array()}} to convert
any of these into the long-format \code{data} that
\code{mvgam(family = occ())} / \code{jsdgam(family = occ())} expect, with
\code{site_covs}, \code{season_covs}, \code{site_season_covs}, and \code{obs_covs}
broadcast across the right grid axes.
}

\section{JSDM with imperfect detection}{

Passing \code{occ()} to \code{\link[=jsdgam]{jsdgam()}} with \code{n_lv > 0} composes the
single-season Bernoulli marginalisation with the Heaps factor
model so the user gets a hierarchical JSDM whose three levels
each live in a distinct dpar:

\describe{
\item{\strong{lowest level}: env-driven latent factors.}{
\code{factor_formula = ~ s(env, by = lv_axis())} makes each
latent factor a smooth of an environmental covariate, so
the factors track env gradients rather than being free
draws.}
\item{\strong{middle level}: species loadings on occupancy.}{Each
species \code{s} loads on the \code{K} factors via the row
\verb{Z[s, :]}, so
\verb{logit_psi[s, i] = b_X(species) + Z[s, :] \%*\% lv[i, :]}
for site \code{i}. \code{Z} is identified up to sign via Heaps and
Jermyn (2024) post-hoc QR.}
\item{\strong{top level}: imperfect detection.}{The \code{p} dpar
carries its own brms sub-formula (e.g.,
\code{bf(y ~ species, p ~ s(tod))}) so the per-visit detection
process is modelled independently of the latent occupancy
state. The lpmf marginalises latent \code{z} per closure unit;
nothing about the factor model has to be aware of the
marginalisation, and nothing about the marginalisation has
to be aware of the factor model.}
}

Recovery on this composition is documented in
\code{tests/local/jsdgam_mv_occ.R}. See \code{\link[=jsdgam]{jsdgam()}} for the
wrapper-level API and \code{\link[=lv_axis]{lv_axis()}} for the \code{by = lv_axis()}
sentinel that turns smooths into per-factor regressors.
}

\section{Cross-reference with ubms / spOccupancy / flocker}{

mvgam's \code{occ()} uses the long-form ecology vocabulary
(\code{occupancy}, \code{detection}) in \code{predict(type = ...)}. The
equivalents in adjacent packages:
\itemize{
\item ubms
(\url{https://github.com/biodiverse/ubms}):
\code{predict(submodel = "state")} returns marginal psi;
\code{predict(submodel = "det")} returns p;
\code{posterior_predict(param = "z")} returns 0/1 latent
occupancy draws conditioned on the observed history.
\item spOccupancy
(\url{https://github.com/biodiverse/spOccupancy}):
\code{psi.0.samples} (marginal psi), \code{z.0.samples} (latent z
draws).
\item flocker
(\url{https://github.com/jsocolar/flocker}):
\code{fitted_flocker(components = "occ" | "det")} for linpred
extraction; \code{get_Z(history_condition = TRUE)} for
conditional z draws.
}

mvgam: \code{predict(fit, type = "latent_state")} returns the
conditional probability \code{P(z = 1 | y)} per site;
\code{posterior_occupancy(fit, conditional = TRUE, draw = TRUE)}
returns 0/1 z draws; \code{posterior_occupancy(conditional = FALSE)}
returns marginal psi. \code{predict(fit, type = "detection")}
returns the per-visit detection probability p_{g,j} on the
response scale.
}

\examples{
\donttest{
# Single-species occupancy fit with separate covariates on
# the occupancy (psi) and detection (p) sub-formulas. The
# closure-unit grain is (series, time) -- 50 sites, 4 visits
# each.
set.seed(4)
simdat <- sim_closure_unit_data(family = occ(), n_species = 1L,
                                  n_sites = 50L, n_visits = 4L,
                                  type = 1L)

mod <- mvgam(
  bf(y ~ env, p ~ tod_c),
  data    = simdat$data_train,
  family  = occ(),
  chains  = 2,
  silent  = 2
)
summary(mod, include_betas = FALSE)

# Marginal env effect on the response scale (occupancy *
# detection). For the logit-occupancy view pass
# `type = "link"`.
conditional_effects(mod)

# Closure-unit post-fit surface. `predict(type = "latent_state")`
# returns posterior summaries of the latent occupancy probability
# psi at each unit; `predict(type = "detection")` returns the
# per-visit detection probability p. Both are confounded in the
# raw 0/1 record and only separable under the marginalised
# occupancy likelihood.
head(predict(mod, type = "latent_state"))
head(predict(mod, type = "detection"))

# `hindcast(type = "latent_state")` returns the full per-draw
# posterior on psi as an `mvgam_latent_state` object with
# `as.data.frame()` and a faceted `plot()` for direct inspection
# and ggplot composition.
hc <- hindcast(mod, type = "latent_state")
print(hc)
plot(hc)

# `pp_check(type = "fit_stat", ...)` runs a closure-unit
# goodness-of-fit test: collapse to per-unit sufficient
# statistics, compare observed vs replicated under the
# Freeman-Tukey or chi-squared discrepancy of MacKenzie &
# Bailey (2004). Returns an `mvgam_ppc_fit_stat` object with
# the Bayesian p-value; values near 0 or 1 indicate poor fit.
pp_check(mod, type = "fit_stat", stat = "freeman_tukey",
          ndraws = 200L)
}

}
